    "result_text": "All tests pass (263 run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`: emits a line to the SLF4J logger named `NOTIFY` containing the owner id and `memberId`, mirroring the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern. It reads the `@Val Owner`, which by that point in the pipeline has both its persisted id (from `SaveOwner`) and its `memberId` (from `AssignMemberId`).\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `notify` step between `audit` and `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the create pipeline, so it only runs on a successful create.\n\nThe captured log confirms the behavior, e.g. `NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`, which satisfies the test's assertion that a NOTIFY line contains both the id and the memberId.",
